 "beats": [
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "A light is floating over the bog. It wants you to follow it. Don't.",
   "cam": "close:odo",
   "do": [
    [
     "w1",
     "drift:-3,9,2.0"
    ],
    [
     "odo",
     "shake"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "DON'T FOLLOW THE LIGHT"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "For hundreds of years, people in England and Ireland wrote down the same warning.",
   "cam": "two:odo,moth",
   "do": [
    [
     "moth",
     "shake"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "A REAL WARNING"
  },
  {
   "who": "odo",
   "say": "Mothwick... that light just moved closer.",
   "cam": "close:odo",
   "do": [
    [
     "odo",
     "turn:moth"
    ],
    [
     "w1",
     "drift:-4.5,8,1.9"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "who": "moth",
   "say": "Lights don't move on their own, Odo. Do they?",
   "cam": "close:moth",
   "do": [
    [
     "moth",
     "eyes_big"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "They called it the will-o'-the-wisp. A wisp was a bundle of sticks, burned as a torch.",
   "cam": "overhead",
   "text": "WILL-O'-THE-WISP"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "Scholars gave it a Latin name, ignis fatuus. The foolish fire.",
   "cam": "prop:w1",
   "do": [
    [
     "w1",
     "bounce"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "THE FOOLISH FIRE"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "And every story says the same thing. The light leads travellers off the path.",
   "cam": "close:trav",
   "do": [
    [
     "trav",
     "enter:left"
    ]
   ],
   "sfx": "suspicious"
  },
  {
   "who": "trav",
   "say": "A lantern! Someone's out there. Hello? Wait for me!",
   "cam": "close:trav",
   "do": [
    [
     "trav",
     "turn:front"
    ],
    [
     "w2",
     "show"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "But every time he stepped closer, the light floated farther away.",
   "cam": "wide",
   "do": [
    [
     "trav",
     "to:0,11"
    ],
    [
     "w2",
     "drift:5,16,1.8"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "Closer. Farther. Closer. Farther. Until the ground under his feet turned to water.",
   "cam": "close:trav",
   "do": [
    [
     "trav",
     "to:3,13"
    ],
    [
     "w2",
     "drift:9,21,1.6"
    ],
    [
     "trav",
     "shake"
    ]
   ],
   "sfx": "suspicious",
   "text": "THE GROUND IS WATER"
  },
  {
   "who": "moth",
   "say": "That is why you never follow it.",
   "cam": "close:moth",
   "do": [
    [
     "moth",
     "turn:odo"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "In Shropshire, England, they told of a wicked blacksmith called Will.",
   "cam": "overhead",
   "do": [
    [
     "trav",
     "exit"
    ],
    [
     "w2",
     "vanish"
    ],
    [
     "w1",
     "vanish"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "The tale says even the Devil sent him away, and threw him one burning coal.",
   "cam": "prop:coal",
   "do": [
    [
     "coal",
     "show"
    ]
   ],
   "sfx": "suspicious"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "So Will wanders the marshes forever, using that coal to lure people into the mud.",
   "cam": "prop:coal",
   "do": [
    [
     "coal",
     "bounce"
    ]
   ],
   "text": "WILL WANDERS FOREVER"
  },
  {
   "who": "narr",
   "say": "In Ireland, the light had another name. Jack-o'-lantern.",
